.25 (20-23), 0.63 (24-27), 0.16 (28-31), 0.25 (32-34), 0.16 (35-45).\n\nWait DN20: models 11–14 (Q3=2.5) → 0.16; models 15–19 (Q3=4) → 0.25. Yes.\n\nNow the matrix table rows mirror the same.\n\nOne more consideration: pressure_loss attribute name: \"pressure_loss_delta_p\" — avoid Δ (non-LaTeX but Greek; canonical label snake_case; I'll use \"pressure_loss\" with description, or \"pressure_loss_class\". Tables say \"Pressure loss class ΔP\" (Tab1) and \"Pressure loss ΔP\". Use attribute \"pressure_loss_delta_p\" — contains letters only. OK.\n\nratio_q3_q1 label: fine.\n\nPermanent flowrate q3: \"permanent_flowrate_q3\". min: \"minimum_flowrate_q1\", trans: \"transitional_flowrate_q2\", overload: \"overload_flowrate_q4\".\n\nAlso there's \"flowrate_q3_and_ratio_marking\" — skip.\n\nNow write the final JSON. Size will be large (~45 models × several arrays). Acceptable.\n\nFor matrix_tables rows, use short keys: dn, q3_m3h? Better: columns list gives names and units, rows use the column names as keys: {\"nominal_diameter\": 15, \"permanent_flowrate_q3\": 1.6, \"minimum_flowrate_q1\": 0.02, \"transitional_flowrate_q2\": 0.032, \"overload_flowrate_q4\": 2, \"ratio_q3_q1\": 80, \"pressure_loss_delta_p\": 0.16, \"connection_thread\": \"G 3/4\", \"construction_length_mm\": [80,105,110,115,165,170]}.\n\ncolumn_units: [null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, \"bar\", null, \"mm\"].\n\nInclude construction_length_mm as array — fine for JSON.\n\nDescription per table: e.g. \"QALCOSONIC W1, DN15, design A and design B; all variants accuracy class 2...\" Keep short: \"DN15 variants of QALCOSONIC W1. Common data: ratio Q2/Q1 = 1.6; installation horizontal/vertical; temperature classes T30, T50, T30/70, T70; MAP 16 bar; MPE ±2% (T≤30°C), ±3% (T>30°C), ±5% (Q1≤Q<Q2); scale interval 0.001 m³; battery li 3.6 V, 16 years.\" Maybe too repetitive; brief is fine.\n\nFootnotes: none — omit the field.\n\nrevision_history dates: \"2023-01-13\", \"2023-05-25\", \"2024-05-31\", \"2025-01-28\".\n\nchanges strings:\n- \"0\": \"Certificate first issued\"\n- \"1\": \"Point 2.4 Software specification – supplemented specification for all DNs separately\"\n- \"2\": \"Issued updated Evaluation Report No: 2022/ER010/SK1_ Rev. 1\"\n- \"3\": \"Add design B (DN15 and DN20); Changed address of the issuing authority SLM on the EU-type examination certificate\"\n\nissuing_authority.website/phone/email: not present — omit.\n\ncertificate.oiml_issuer_id: \"SK1\". Also issuing_authority.oiml_issuer_id \"SK1\".\n\ncertified_type.category: \"Water meter\".\n\nType designations: [\"Qalcosonic W1\"] — also \"QALCOSONIC W1\". I'll include both spellings? They're the same type; listing both could be seen as duplicates. The instruction: \"all type/model identifiers mentioned\". I'll list [\"Qalcosonic W1\", \"QALCOSONIC W1\"]? Hmm, redundant. I'll just use \"Qalcosonic W1\". Actually the technical sections consistently use \"QALCOSONIC W1\"; the ID table uses \"Qalcosonic W1\". One canonical: \"Qalcosonic W1\". Fine.\n\ndescription: compose.\n\nLet me draft description: \"The QALCOSONIC W1 is a compact ultrasonic water meter with electronic indication device, designed to measure, memorise and display the volume of clean water passing through the measurement transducer at metering conditions (residential use, non-resettable measurements). Measurement is based on the ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time principle. The meter can be installed in horizontal and vertical positions and is not designed to measure reverse flow. Produced in A design (all DN) and B design (DN15 and DN20 only); the difference lies solely in the external appearance, the measurement section being identical. Non-essential parts: antenna; non-return valve (optional).\"\n\nconfig_level:\n\n[\n {\n  \"attribute\": \"water_temperature_range\",\n  \"axis\": \"meter_temperature_class\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"T30\", \"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 30}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"T50\", \"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"T30/70\", \"value\": {\"min\": 30, \"max\": 70}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"T70\", \"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 70}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"attribute\": \"maximum_permitted_error_upper_zone\",\n  \"axis\": \"water_temperature\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"water temperature ≤ 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -2, \"max\": 2}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"water temperature > 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -3, \"max\": 3}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"attribute\": \"connection_thread\",\n  \"axis\": \"nominal_diameter\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"DN15\", \"value\": \"G 3/4\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN20\", \"value\": \"G 1\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN25\", \"value\": \"G 1 1/4\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN32\", \"value\": \"G 1 1/2\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN40\", \"value\": \"G 2\"}\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"attribute\": \"construction_length\",\n  \"axis\": \"nominal_diameter\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"DN15\", \"value\": \"80, 105, 110, 115, 165, 170\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN20\", \"value\": \"105, 110, 130, 165, 190\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN25\", \"value\": \"260\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN32\", \"value\": \"260\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"DN40\", \"value\": \"300\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"}\n  ]\n }\n]\n\nHmm, construction length could be value arrays [80,105,...]. Rule: value number|range|string. String of list is safest.\n\nAlso MPE lower zone in type_level as {min:-5,max:5}.\n\nAlso battery configs per DN — config_level? axis \"nominal_diameter + design\". The text is muddled; I'll put a summary string in components. Skip config_level for batteries.\n\nNow type_level values with unit_symbol/unit_id:\n\n{\n \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n \"mechanical_class\": {\"value\": \"M1\", ...},\n \"climatic_class\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -15, \"max\": 70}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\", \"unit_id\": \"u:degree_Celsius\"},\n \"electromagnetic_class\": {\"value\": \"E2\"},\n \"environmental_classification\": {\"value\": \"B/O\"},\n \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\": {\"value\": \"U0D0\"},\n \"installation_position\": {\"value\": \"Horizontal / Vertical\"},\n \"meter_temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T30, T50, T30/70, T70\"},\n \"maximum_working_pressure_map\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar\"},\n \"ratio_q2_q1\": {\"value\": 1.6},\n \"maximum_permitted_error_lower_zone\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -5, \"max\": 5}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n \"scale_interval\": {\"value\": 0.001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n \"scale_interval_testing_mode\": {\"value\": 0.000001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n \"calculator_capacity\": {\"value\": 999999.999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n \"calculator_capacity_testing_mode\": {\"value\": 999.999999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n \"battery_chemistry\": {\"value\": \"lithium\"},\n \"battery_voltage\": {\"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n \"battery_lifetime\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"years\"},\n \"integrated_communication_interfaces\": {\"value\": \"Wireless M-Bus, LoRa, NFC, NB-IoT radio\"},\n \"microcontroller\": {\"value\": \"Renesas RF10WMGAFB MCU (128 KB) or Renesas R5F111PJGFB MCU (256 KB)\"}\n}\n\nComponents:\n\n[\n {\n  \"role\": \"flow sensor (measurement transducer)\",\n  \"type_designations\": [],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"body\": \"plastic cylindrical brass body with inlet and outlet firmly connected with the plastic housing for the calculator\",\n    \"sound_path\": \"inner plastic element with two mirrors (four mirrors for DN40)\",\n    \"ultrasonic_transducers\": \"two (four for DN40) placed on the upside of the cylindrical plastic body\",\n    \"measurement_principle\": \"ultrasonic, bidirectional transit-time\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"role\": \"calculator and indication device\",\n  \"type_designations\": [],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"housing\": \"plastic housing directly mounted on the flow sensor\",\n    \"electronics\": \"three PCBs and one PCB with calculator\",\n    \"display\": \"electronic LCD, 2 lines: upper line 9 digits with indication range 999999.999 m³; lower line 5 digits for current flow rate in m³/h\",\n    \"batteries\": \"non-replaceable lithium batteries, life 16 years\",\n    \"battery_configuration\": \"DN15/DN20/DN25/DN32: two AA batteries; DN15/DN20 (design B): one C + one A23; DN40: one D (+ one A23)\"\n  }\n }\n]\n\nAlternatives field not needed (omit).\n\ntest_reports as above.\n\nrecommendation: {\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [2]}.\n\nShould recommendation include amendment? Omit.\n\ncertificate object:\n{\n \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02 Rev. 3\",\n \"scheme\": \"A\",\n \"page_total\": 13,\n \"member_state\": \"Slovakia\",\n \"date_issued\": \"2025-01-28\",\n \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"SK1\"\n}\nOmit project_number.\n\nNow, write everything. Be careful with JSON validity: no trailing commas, proper escaping. Use plain UTF-8 characters (°, ³, ≤). JSON allows them.\n\nLet me also decide whether to include \"column_units\" — schema example includes it. Yes.\n\nmatrix_tables[0]:\n{\n \"name\": \"Tab. 1 – Technical and metrological data, DN15\",\n \"columns\": [\"nominal_diameter\", \"permanent_flowrate_q3\", \"minimum_flowrate_q1\", \"transitional_flowrate_q2\", \"overload_flowrate_q4\", \"ratio_q3_q1\", \"pressure_loss_delta_p\", \"connection_thread\", \"construction_length_mm\"],\n \"column_units\": [null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null, \"bar\", null, \"mm\"],\n \"rows\": [10 rows],\n \"description\": \"QALCOSONIC W1, nominal diameter DN15 (designs A and B).\"\n}\n\nRows DN15:\n{\"nominal_diameter\": 15, \"permanent_flowrate_q3\": 1.6, \"minimum_flowrate_q1\": 0.02,