ts\": [{...}],\n  \"manufacturers\": [{...}],\n  \"certified_type\": {...},\n  \"model_family\": {...},\n  \"components\": [...],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n     \"type_level\": {...},\n     \"model_level\": [...],\n     \"config_level\": [...]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {...},\n  \"test_reports\": [...],\n  \"revision_history\": [...]\n}\n\nDouble-check date formats: use ISO \"2025-01-28\" for dates. Report \"dated 28st January 2025\" → 2025-01-28. Doc file 1: 13th January 2023 → 2023-01-13. Doc file 2: 28st January 2025 → 2025-01-28.\n\nWrite it out now. Careful: JSON must not include comments.\n\nOne more check: \"Maximum permissible error in upper flowrates range Q₂ ≤ Q ≤ Q₄\" label → maximum_permitted_error_upper_zone. And lower → maximum_permitted_error_lower_zone.\n\nAlso attribute for accuracy class 2: value 2 numeric? I'll use \"2\" as number 2. In recommendation accuracy_classes: [2]? Hmm — I'll use [2]? Actually many implementations use strings; but number is fine. Keep [2]? Let me use [\"2\"]? Decision: numbers [2]. Hmm wait — \"class 2\" vs \"class 1\" numeric is fine. Go [2].\n\nHmm, one subtlety: type_level key names — use canonical snake_case labels as keys: e.g. \"maximum_capacity\": {...}. So type_level object with keys like \"accuracy_class\". Good.\n\nFor model_level entries, follow example format: {\"attribute\": \"qmax\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5}, ...]}.\n\nNow count effort for 7 attributes × 45 = 315 short objects. Fine.\n\nLet me write model_ids as e.g. \"DN15_Q3=1.6_R80\". Consistent.\n\nBegin JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02 Rev. 3\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"page_total\": 13,\n    \"member_state\": \"Slovakia\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2025-01-28\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"SK1\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Slovak Legal Metrology (SLM)\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\n      \"Geologická 9966/1, 821 06 Bratislava-Podunajské Biskupice, Slovakia\",\n      \"Product Certification Body, Hviezdoslavova 31, 974 01 Banská Bystrica, Slovakia\"\n    ],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Ing. Dušan Šmigura, PhD.\",\n    \"person_title\": \"Director of PCB\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"SK1\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"UAB „Axioma Metering“\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Veterinaru str. 52, Biruliskes, LT-54469 Kaunas region, Lithuania\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"UAB „Axioma Metering“\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Veterinaru str. 52, Biruliskes, LT-54469 Kaunas region, Lithuania\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"Qalcosonic W1\"],\n    \"module_designation\": \"Ultrasonic water meters with electronic indication device\",\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  ...\n}\n\nApplicant name contains „ “ quotes — keep as in doc? JSON fine with Unicode. Keep \"UAB „Axioma Metering“\". Maybe normalize to \"UAB Axioma Metering\". I'll keep the quotes as printed — harmless.\n\nDescription text (concise):\n\"The ultrasonic water meter type QALCOSONIC W1 is a compact water meter with electronic indication device designed to measure, memorise and display the volume of clean water passing through the measurement transducer at metering conditions (residential use, non-resettable measurements). Measurement is based on the ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time principle. The meter can be installed in horizontal and vertical positions and is not designed to measure reverse flow. It is produced in A design (all DNs) and design B (DN15 and DN20 only); the difference lies solely in the external appearance, the measurement section being identical. Non-essential parts: antenna; non-return valve (optional).\"\n\nOK now write everything out fully.\n\nFor matrix table descriptions:\nTab1: \"QALCOSONIC W1, DN15 (designs A and B). Connection thread G 3/4; construction lengths 80, 105, 110, 115, 165, 170 mm.\"\nTab2: \"... DN20 ... G 1; lengths 105, 110, 130, 165, 190 mm.\"\nTab3: \"DN25 ... G 1 1/4; length 260 mm.\"\nTab4: \"DN32 ... G 1 1/2; length 260 mm.\"\nTab5: \"DN40 ... G 2; length 300 mm. Flow sensor with four mirrors and four ultrasonic transducers for DN40.\"\nSoftware: description \"Software version indicated on data plate as SW:x.xx; checksum as indicated.\"\n\nEverything set — write final JSON. Ensure no trailing commas and all braces closed. This will be long; be disciplined.",
